    "posts": [
      {
        "number": 1,
        "text": "A Web3 portfolio needs a path from claim to evidence. For each project, show the problem, your contribution and something a reviewer can inspect. A title like 'growth lead' leaves all of that unanswered.",
        "alt": "Make your work inspectable. Problem. Your contribution. Evidence.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/C01-01.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 2,
        "text": "For an engineering sample, include a README with setup steps and tests for failure cases. Example: a withdrawal test should check what happens when the caller lacks permission, not only when the transfer succeeds.",
        "alt": "Show the failure case. Allowed caller. Rejected caller. Test command. Known limits.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/C01-02.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 3,
        "text": "For a marketing sample, write a campaign brief with an audience, a user action and a measurement plan. Example: a wallet tutorial can measure setup completion. Impressions alone won't tell you whether readers finished setup.",
        "alt": "Connect content to an action. Tutorial reader. Setup attempt. Setup completion. Measurement limits.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/C01-03.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 4,
        "text": "For community or operations work, show the system you built. A sample support runbook could explain how to collect an error report, assign an owner and tell the user when to expect an update.",
        "alt": "Document a repeatable task. Error report. Assigned owner. Next update. Resolution record.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/C01-04.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 5,
        "text": "Private work can still make a useful case study. Describe the constraint and your decision using approved, redacted material. Label a personal exercise as an exercise; don't turn it into a fictional client project.",
        "alt": "Label the evidence honestly. Public work. Approved redaction. Personal exercise.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/C01-05.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 6,
        "text": "Before applying, open every portfolio link while logged out. Put the most relevant sample first, name your part in it and explain one limitation. A reviewer should be able to follow the evidence without requesting access.\n\nhashtagweb3.com/building-web3-portfolio/th",
        "alt": "Run the reviewer check. Logged-out access. Relevant sample first. Authorship clear. Limits stated.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/C01-06.jpg"
      }
    ],
